**Definition 1.3 (complete targets and error).** Put

$$
\begin{aligned}
\varsigma_y&=y/(y+6),& f_y(t)&=6y/(y+6t)^2,\\
d_y&=\left(y/128,\frac{y(58-y)}{128(y+6)},\frac{y}{2(y+6)}\right),&
(B_y)_{ij}&=\sqrt{d_{yi}d_{yj}},\\
w&=(0,1/4,1/2,1/4,0),&P_f&=|f\rangle\langle f|.
\end{aligned}
\tag{CA.5}
$$

The target $\Omega_{y,e,n}$ has live block
$EU_{e,n}B_yU_{e,n}^\dagger E^\dagger$ and, separately at each original
label $j$, the measure $w_j f_y(t)dt\,P_f$. Exact time is elapsed
$t\in[0,1]$, equivalently absolute time $6+t$. Labels $1,3$ stay distinct;
$0,13$ stay named zero-density sectors. The target has live trace
$\varsigma_y$ and failure trace $1-\varsigma_y$.

The original common processor receives only the sole specimen and fixed
common metadata/blanks, calibration, source/epoch identity, permissions,
controller and aligned clock. There is no readable history, waveform,
